      "model": {
        "model_architecture": "mobilenet_v3_small",
        "description": "Lightweight CPU-friendly image classifier designed for mobile/edge devices; small footprint and fast inference on CPU cores. Suitable for 224x224 input, can be fine-tuned on SOP-like data, and fits the 1.5 GB runtime memory target with CPU-only deployment.",
        "architecture_family": "mobilenet"
      }
    },
    "rationale": "Given the CPU-only backend (4 cores, 8 GB RAM), the priority is a strong memory-latency trade-off while still achieving macro-F1 >= 0.85. Mobilenet_v3_small offers the smallest runtime memory and likely sub-500 ms inference on typical 224x224 inputs, making it the most robust fit under the hard memory constraint and latency target. It supports efficient transfer learning and quantization, which helps meet accuracy goals on the provided five-class furniture dataset. EfficientNet-B0 could offer higher accuracy but carries greater risk of higher latency and memory consumption on CPU, which could threaten the 500 ms target and 1.5 GB runtime memory cap. If macro-F1 remains below 0.85 during validation, a fallback to EfficientNet-B0 (or another more-capable architecture) can be attempted, with careful quantization and pruning to meet constraints.",
