    "rationale": "Target per-class pool: 1500 images per class, totaling 7500 images across chair/sofa/table/cabinet/lamp. All selections use the training split from Stanford Online Products (SOP_cls_train) as the primary source for each class, which satisfies the requirement to use training sources for the primary pool and provides coherent, multi-class coverage from a single dataset family. Reasoning by class and source: SOP_cls_train has ample per-class examples for all five furniture-related categories (chair, sofa, table, cabinet, lamp), with available counts well above 1500 per class, so no scarcity constraints are triggered. CIFAR-100 options are avoided here due to domain semantics (general objects and low-resolution imagery) and to maintain domain alignment with product photography. By using SOP_cls_train exclusively, we maximize domain coherence (product/fine-grained imagery) and reduce leakage risk across domains or annotation schemes, while meeting the target macro-F1 and latency constraints when fine-tuning a lightweight CPU-friendly model such as mobilenet_v3_small. Approximate total training pool size selected: 1500 images per class \u00d7 5 classes = 7500 images. This is comfortably within typical budget expectations and well below the stated practical limits (and far below the 10k per class / 50k total guidance). The default download budget does not constrain this plan, as the chosen counts are supported by the available training samples for SOP_cls_train. Final train/validation/test splits will be derived deterministically from these pools during model training; the output describes only the primary per-class training pools.",
